<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <!--
            Remove the duplicate "My Extensions" link Blue_LicenseDelivery adds to
            the account navigation. This package's own My Extensions block is the
            one that should be there.

            WHY hyva_default AND NOT hyva_customer_account, which is where this
            obviously belongs:

            Hyvä mirrors handles with a hyva_ prefix in two places -
            AddLayoutHandles (layout_load_before) copies the addHandle-registered
            handles, and AddLayoutHandlesUpdates (load_file_layout_updates_xml_after)
            copies every <update handle="X"/> node. `customer_account` is NOT a
            page handle: nothing in vendor/magento calls addHandle for it, it is
            reached only through <update handle="customer_account"/>. So
            `hyva_customer_account` exists ONLY by the second observer.

            Measured: it does work on the Hyvä installed here (1.5.2). But
            composer.json requires hyva-themes/magento2-theme-module at "*", so
            this package installs against versions predating that observer, and
            on one of those the file would be inert - silently restoring the
            duplicate link with nothing to indicate it.

            `default` is always in getHandles(), so `hyva_default` is mirrored by
            the FIRST observer and works on every Hyvä that supports the prefix
            convention at all. A referenceBlock remove for a block that is not on
            the page is a no-op, so applying it site-wide costs nothing.

            Probed both directions before relying on it: the handle applies on
            the Hyvä store view and does NOT apply on the Luma one.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="customer-account-link-license-extensions" remove="true"/>
    </body>
</page>
